# Python bytecode. Build output, never source.
#
# A stray tools/__pycache__/*.pyc was staged during the work that added
# bundle/scope.json, and the scope check caught it on its first run. The check
# is the backstop; this file is the reason it should not have to fire.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Release archives. Build output of tools/build-archive.sh, and untracked
# build output is not harmless here: sign-release.sh refuses to sign a dirty
# tree and sync.sh marks one, so a maintainer who built an archive locally
# would find the next release blocked by files the build had just made.
dist/
